macOS espeak-ng dead-strip note
--------------------------------

The prebuilt static archive contains libespeak-ng.a, but Apple ld's atom-level dead stripping
removed the unused TTS path from the measured macOS arm64 binary: `nm` found no `espeak_*` or
`OfflineTts*` symbols, and `strings` found no `espeak-ng-data` string. This is a platform-specific
result. The same archive linked on Linux retained espeak-ng code; a Linux or Windows release must
repeat the license gate and must not assume the macOS result applies.
